// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// FRONTIER & PHILOSOPHY VOYAGER  |  L20 — CAPSTONE: Writing Your Personal Philosophy
// Age band : voyagers (11-12)   Guide: orion (Phoenix)
// Standards: Coreverse Original — Philosophy (capstone synthesis across the whole band)
// CALIBRATED: Voyager spec v1.1 (May 2026)
//
// SUBJECT NOTE — Frontier & Philosophy (CAPSTONE):
//   - This is the FINAL lesson of the band. It weaves together everything from L01-L19 into the
//     learner's OWN personal philosophy: a coherent, examined way of seeing and living that's
//     truly theirs. Pulls the recurring threads: clear thinking & logic, knowledge & evidence,
//     ethics, identity/self, meaning, intellectual humility & steelmanning, evenhandedness, the
//     manipulation-detection spine (the universal control/unfalsifiability fingerprints), and
//     "wonder + clear eyes" together.
//   - TONE: celebratory, empowering, warm, identity-forming. This is a graduation. The learner is
//     the author. The protective spine is reframed positively: you now carry tools that make you
//     genuinely hard to fool and free to think for yourself.
//   - The "argument" being built here is not a proof of a contested claim but the learner's own
//     reasoned stance on how to think and live well — assembled from principle-blocks earned
//     across the band. No single correct order; modelArgument shows one strong, coherent assembly.
//   - Honesty: emphasize that a personal philosophy is held with conviction AND humility, revisable
//     with new evidence — not dogma. Em-dashes natural; do NOT run em-dash replacement.
//
//   CAPSTONE SPECIFICS (per spec): xpReward 100, celebration.xpEarned 100,
//   celebration.nextLessonPreview = null (band complete).
//
// Interaction format: ARGUMENT-BUILDER (screen 7). Audited contract (NOT verified vs shipped file
// in this working dir): {id,type,headline,intro,claim,blocks:[{id,text,type}],modelArgument,
// reflectionPrompt}. block.type in premise|evidence|objection|response|conclusion. If player
// reports stuck / no Continue on install, verify field names vs player source.
//
// QUIZ STANDARD (locked): 8 MC + 1 TF + 1 inference. Short options, comparable length, plausible
// distractors, correct rotated/not-longest; teaching in `explanation`. Quiz reviews the band's
// core tools (a fitting capstone check).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

